[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Kernel Clock and Timing
PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-10-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: System Tick and Uptime

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-7
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Configurable system tick frequency
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support a configurable system tick frequency that determines the
resolution of kernel time-based services.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to configure the system tick rate to match the timing
requirements of my application.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: System uptime in milliseconds
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to read the elapsed time since system startup
in milliseconds.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to query the current system uptime in milliseconds in order
to implement time-based logic in my application.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-9
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: 32-bit system uptime interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to read the lower 32 bits of the elapsed time
since system startup in milliseconds.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-10
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Uptime delta calculation
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to calculate the elapsed time in milliseconds
between a reference time and the current uptime.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Hardware Cycle Counter

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-11
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: 32-bit hardware cycle counter
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to read the current value of the hardware
cycle counter as a 32-bit value.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want a high-resolution hardware counter for measuring short
durations with sub-millisecond precision.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-12
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: 64-bit hardware cycle counter
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to read the current value of the hardware
cycle counter as a 64-bit value when supported by the hardware.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Thread Sleep and Delay

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-13
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Thread sleep for a timeout duration
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to put the current thread into a sleeping
state for a specified timeout duration, yielding the CPU to other threads.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want my thread to be able to sleep for a specified duration
and be automatically woken up when the duration expires.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-14
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Thread sleep in milliseconds
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to put the current thread into a sleeping
state for a specified number of milliseconds.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-15
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Thread sleep in microseconds
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to put the current thread into a sleeping
state for a specified number of microseconds.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-16
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Busy-wait delay
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to spin-wait for a specified number of
microseconds without yielding the CPU.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want a busy-wait function for short, precise delays where
blocking the thread is not acceptable (e.g. within an ISR or critical section).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-17
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Waking a sleeping thread early
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to wake a sleeping thread before its sleep
timeout expires and return the remaining sleep time to the caller.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Timeout Specification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-18
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: No-wait timeout constant
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a timeout constant that specifies a zero-duration wait,
causing the calling interface to return immediately if the requested resource or condition
is not available.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-19
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Wait-forever timeout constant
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a timeout constant that specifies an indefinite wait,
causing the calling interface to block until the resource or condition becomes available.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-20
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Timeout specified in milliseconds
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to specify a timeout value in milliseconds.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-21
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Timeout specified in microseconds
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to specify a timeout value in microseconds.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-10-22
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Timeout specified in system ticks
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to specify a timeout value in system ticks.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-27

[[/SECTION]]
